# Stage 7b's criterion (TASK-24, docs/research/desktop/plan.md): the GUI
# test moves, minimises, restores and closes a terminal window over QMP,
# switches with Alt+Tab and F12, and passes at both scales. Coordinates
# are logical: the terminal's frame is at (72, 70), 670 wide, its title bar
# 36 high, the close cross at (90, 88) and the minimise dash at (114, 88)
# (ADR-0160; zoraya_compositor::ORIGIN under the 28-pixel bar).
serial init: gui: gpu on its own page
screen Type help to begin, or help tour.
screen ~> _
region 130 76 200 4 f7f7f8
region 72 120 1 300 d7d9de
shot windows-start
# Moved by its title bar, (100, 50) and back.
drag 300 88 400 138
region 230 126 200 4 f7f7f8
region 172 170 1 300 d7d9de
drag 400 138 300 88
region 130 76 200 4 f7f7f8
# Minimised by the dash; F12 brings it back, and it takes keys again.
click 114 88
key f12
type echo restored\r
screen restored
screen ~> _
# Minimised again; Alt+Tab (the switcher, chosen on Alt's release) brings
# it back.
click 114 88
chord alt tab
type echo switched\r
screen switched
screen ~> _
# Closed by the cross: the terminal ends, and init opens a new one with a
# new shell, as after exit.
click 90 88
serial init: the terminal was closed
window
screen Type help to begin, or help tour.
screen ~> _
# A new window takes focus only from the person (ADR-0094): its title bar,
# then its focused ground, before any key (on CI's slower runner the keys
# otherwise reached no window, 2026-11-09).
click 400 80
region 130 76 100 4 f7f7f8
type poweroff\r
exit
